   "ageDays": 0.0,
   "summary": "Iqbal , an elected Member of Parliament (MP), thanked President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. for what he called a “clear and unequivocal commitment” to respect the Parliament’s authority to choose its own leadership under the Bangsamoro Organic Law (BOL). READ: Gov’t keeps hands off BARMM parliament leadership vote “This assurance goes to the heart of what our people struggled for,” Iqbal said in reaction to Sarmiento’s statement.",
   "summary_zh": "当选议员伊克巴尔感谢费迪南德·马科斯小总统对他所说的“明确且毫不含糊的承诺”，即尊重议会根据《邦萨摩洛组织法》（BOL）自行选择领导层的权力。阅读：政府不干预BARMM议会领导层投票 “这一保证触及我们人民为之奋斗的核心，”伊克巴尔在回应萨缅托的声明时表示。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Iqbal , an elected Member of Parliament (MP), thanked President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. for what he called a “clear and unequivocal commitment” to respect the Parliament’s authority to choose its own leadership under the Bangsamoro Organic Law (BOL). READ: Gov’t keeps hands off BARMM parliament leadership vote “This assurance goes to the heart of what our people struggled for,” Iqbal said in reaction to Sarmiento’s statement. Iqbal said the Comprehensive Agreement on the Bangsamoro (CAB) and the BOL were meant to give substance to the Bangsamoro people’s right to self-determination, including the right to choose their leaders through their elected representatives. “When the Members of Parliament gather after taking their oath on October 30 to elect the Chief Minister, that choice must be theirs, and theirs alone,” he said. Iqbal, who served as the MILF’s chief negotiator in the talks that led to the CAB, said the President’s commitment honors “not only the letter of the law, but the spirit of the peace agreement” signed in good faith by the Government of the Philippines and the MILF. In its statement, OPAPRU cited Marcos’ Oct. 14 remarks following the announcement of a 46-member majority coalition in the 80-seat Parliament, in which the President said he respects the Parliament’s authority to determine its leadership and looks forward to working with the government it constitutes. Sarmiento said the President will reach out to all political parties in the region once the Parliament has chosen its leaders and formed the Government of the Day. “It encompasses the socioeconomic transformation of our former combatants and their communities, transitional justice and reconciliation, and the security arrangements that will allow our people to live in peace and dignity,” he said. Your subscription could not be saved. Please try again. Your subscription has been successful. He also called on his fellow MPs, “regardless of party,” to show that “the Bangsamoro is capable of governing itself with wisdom, unity, and integrity.” /jpv",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ph"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 4,
   "actor": "第三方",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_inquirer",
   "title_zh": "Iqbal欢迎总统府誓言不干预BARMM首席遴选",
   "body_zh": "伊克巴尔，一名当选的国会议员（MP），感谢费迪南德·小马科斯总统对他所称的“明确且毫不含糊的承诺”表示感谢，该承诺尊重议会根据《邦萨摩洛有机法》（BOL）选择自身领导人的权力。阅读：政府不干预BARMM议会领导层投票 “这一保证触及我们人民为之奋斗的核心，”伊克巴尔在回应萨缅托的声明时表示。伊克巴尔说，《邦萨摩洛全面协议》（CAB）和BOL旨在赋予邦萨摩洛人民自决权以实质内容，包括通过他们选出的代表选择领导人的权利。“当议员们在10月30日宣誓后聚集起来选举首席部长时，这一选择必须是他们自己的，而且只能是他们自己的，”他说。伊克巴尔曾担任摩洛伊斯兰解放阵线（MILF）在导致CAB谈判中的首席谈判代表，他表示总统的承诺不仅尊重“法律的文字，而且尊重菲律宾政府和MILF本着诚意签署的和平协议的精神”。在其声明中，OPAPRU引用了马科斯10月14日的言论，这些言论是在宣布80席议会中46名多数联盟之后发表的，总统在其中表示他尊重议会决定其领导层的权力，并期待与它所组成的政府合作。萨缅托表示，一旦议会选出其领导人并组建了当日政府，总统将与该地区所有政党接触。“它包括我们前战斗人员及其社区的社会经济转型、过渡正义与和解，以及将使我们人民能够和平而有尊严地生活的安全安排，”他说。您的订阅无法保存。请重试。您的订阅已成功。他还呼吁他的议员同僚“无论党派如何”，都要表现出“邦萨摩洛有能力以智慧、团结和正直的方式管理自己。” /jpv"
