   "published": "Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:28:03 +0800",
   "_dt": 1792470483.0,
   "ageDays": 0.12,
   "summary": "Share in Chat Share article Facebook X (Twitter) Copy Link Copied WHAT YOU NEED TO KNOW The impeachment trial of Vice President Sara Duterte — the first Philippine public official to be impeached twice by the House of Representatives — began at 2 pm on Monday, July 6.",
   "summary_zh": "在聊天中分享 分享文章 Facebook X（Twitter） 复制链接 已复制 需要了解的内容 副总统萨拉·杜特尔特弹劾审判——菲律宾首位被众议院两次弹劾的公职人员——于7月6日星期一下午2点开始。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Share in Chat Share article Facebook X (Twitter) Copy Link Copied WHAT YOU NEED TO KNOW The impeachment trial of Vice President Sara Duterte — the first Philippine public official to be impeached twice by the House of Representatives — began at 2 pm on Monday, July 6. There are four articles of impeachment against Duterte involving alleged misuse of confidential funds, unexplained wealth, bribery of Department of Education officials, and grave threats against President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. and his family. Only 21 out of 24 senator-judges are physically present. Senator Bato dela Rosa remains in hiding as he faces an International Criminal Court arrest warrant over Rodrigo Duterte’s drug war, Senator Jinggoy Estrada has been detained and suspended in connection with a plunder case, and Senator Rodante Marcoleta surrendered to authorities as he also faces a plunder case. On this page, we bring you the latest updates, analyses, videos, and photos as the trial of the Vice President unfolds. House prosecutor Terry Ridon dismisses Vice President Sara Duterte’s remark on “corporate layering” involving Gencorp and Metro City Chow Foods Corporation as a mere excuse, during a press briefing on October 20, 2026. Share in Chat Share article Facebook X (Twitter) Copy Link Copied Oct 14, 2026 2:16 PM PHT Go wants ‘fair’ fight in Sara Duterte trial Rappler.com Senator-judge Bong Go says he wants “fair” fight in the ongoing impeachment trial of Vice President Sara Duterte. Go made the remarks a day after the House prosecution panel dropped three of the four impeachment articles against Duterte. Share in Chat Share article Facebook X (Twitter) Copy Link Copied Oct 14, 2026 11:03 AM PHT Prosecution team holds media briefing | October 14, 2026 Rappler.com The House prosecution team holds a press briefing on Wednesday, October 14, 2026. The possible moves could challenge the prosecution’s reliance on financial forensic analyst Alexander Cabrera’s findings, which the defense claims are based on false assumptions. Rappler multimedia reporter Sundy Locus reports on the defense’s objections, the court’s ruling, and the revised November trial schedule. Share in Chat Share article Facebook X (Twitter) Copy Link Copied Oct 14, 2026 9:00 AM PHT Rappler Recap: Prosecution drops 3 of 4 impeachment articles vs Sara Duterte Dwight de Leon The prosecution withdraws three of the four impeachment articles against Vice President Sara Duterte, leaving unexplained wealth as the sole remaining charge. Rappler multimedia reporter Dwight de Leon recaps and speaks with lead prosecutor Terry Ridon about the decision, the defense’s response, and the prosecution’s confidence in its remaining case. Share in Chat Share article Facebook X (Twitter) Copy Link Copied Oct 13, 2026 6:13 PM PHT Impeachment court announces new Sara Duterte trial schedule Sundy Locus The break in the trial will give way to deliberations on the proposed 2027 budget. The decision drew objections from lead defense counsel Sheila Sison, who warned that abandoning Rule 18 midway through the trial could undermine the integrity of the proceedings. Share in Chat Share article Facebook X (Twitter) Copy Link Copied Load more Loading... Close Pick up right where you left off. Switch to the Rappler app for a smoother, faster reading experience. Upgrade to Rappler+ for exclusive content and unlimited access",
