   "title": "For context.. -this policy simply means the federal government is cutting out the middleman so public universities can hire staff much faste",
   "url": "https://x.com/TheNGCorridor/status/2111850087328411944",
   "snippet": "For context..\n-this policy simply means the federal government is cutting out the middleman so public universities can hire staff much faster.\n\nBEFORE NOW, if a federal university needed to hire a lecturer or replace someone who retired, they had to apply and wait for approval from the Office of the Head of the Civil Service in Abuja. \n\nthat clearance process, known as a waiver\n...it could take months or even years, leaving many departments severely short-staffed!\n\nUnder the new arrangement...Vice-Chancellors and University Governing Councils can advertise and recruit staff directly through the Ministry of Education. \n\nAnd while this speeds up hiring and restores local control to schools, the main worry now is whether university boards will maintain strict merit or open the door to nepotism without central civil service oversight!\n\n@TheNGCorridor",
